messages.content:
Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: png.c
Line: 4007
Function: png_image_error
Bug type: null-pointer-dereference
CWE: CWE-476
Explanation: The function unconditionally dereferences 'image' (image->message) when calling png_safecat without checking if 'image' is NULL. If png_image_error is invoked with a NULL image pointer (e.g., when reporting an error before image initialization), this results in an immediate crash.

Source context:
```c
     3967:    if (c.for_write != 0)
     3968:    {
     3969: #     ifdef PNG_SIMPLIFIED_WRITE_SUPPORTED
     3970:          png_destroy_write_struct(&c.png_ptr, &c.info_ptr);
     3971: #     else
     3972:          png_error(c.png_ptr, "simplified write not supported");
     3973: #     endif
     3974:    }
     3975:    else
     3976:    {
     3977: #     ifdef PNG_SIMPLIFIED_READ_SUPPORTED
     3978:          png_destroy_read_struct(&c.png_ptr, &c.info_ptr, NULL);
     3979: #     else
     3980:          png_error(c.png_ptr, "simplified read not supported");
     3981: #     endif
     3982:    }
     3983: 
     3984:    /* Success. */
     3985:    return 1;
     3986: }
     3987: 
